# The closer the heater, the larger the response, at the price of optical loss in a real device.
# Reference: the same mesh solved with a sparse direct solver in SciPy.
title Heater 1.25 um above the waveguide
grid dx=0.25 dy=0.25
window width=60 ymin=-10 ymax=5
layer si -10 0
layer sio2 0 5
rect si -0.25 0.25 2 2.25
rect tin -1 1 3.5 3.75
heater h xmin=-1 xmax=1 ymin=3.5 ymax=3.75 power=0.1
probe wg xmin=-0.25 xmax=0.25 ymin=2 ymax=2.25
expect response wg h 184.14705 1e-7
expect pi_power wg h 22.6268445 1e-7
expect peak 36.5891348 1e-7
expect balance 1e-9
expect cells 14400
